# Canonical Tailwind classes

Tailwind 4.3 warns (`suggestCanonicalClasses`) when a class has a shorter spelling that emits the same CSS. New classes use that spelling. Leave an existing class until the line is already being edited.

Fixed renames:

| Warning | Write |
|---|---|
| `bg-gradient-to-*` | `bg-linear-to-*` (`t`, `tr`, `r`, `br`, `b`, `bl`, `l`, `tl`) |
| `break-words` | `wrap-break-word` |
| `order-none` | `order-0` |

Same CSS, shorter form:

- A theme utility when an arbitrary value matches it (`p-[16px]` when 16px is on the spacing scale).
- Drop a redundant arbitrary type (`w-[length:1rem]` becomes `w-[1rem]`, or the scale utility).
- Bare variants when they equal the bracket form: `data-open`, `aria-checked`, `supports-display`.
- `*:` for `[&>*]:`, `**:` for `[&_*]:`.
- Omit a modifier that does not change the declaration (`/100` or `/100%` when the result is the unmodified utility).
